## 2. Axiom audit

`axioms.lean` prints `#print axioms` for the relation projections, the reset
lemma, the four unfrozen field lemmas, `bufRelX_step_unfrozen`, the four frozen
field lemmas, `bufRelX_step_frozen`, `frozen_ld_false`, `ld_frozen_hold`, the
two flush-generalised exact-state frozen bridges, the two flush-generalised
relational frozen bridges, the three first-round witness theorems, the seven
landing post-state equations, `modeOf_eq_three`, `ld_frozen_eq`, `rq_frozen_hold`,
`nv_frozen_hold`, `starved_frozen`, the two
`bufRelX_step_frozen_landing` theorems, the two landing witnesses,
`abs_step_frozen_landing` and the two relational landing bridges.  `axioms.txt`
has 43 declarations (45 physical lines, one wrapped):

* 8 `does not depend on any axioms` (the projections and the reset lemmas);
* 35 `depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` or
  `[propext, Quot.sound]`/`[propext]` (the step lemmas, the state bridges and
  the witness theorems);
* no `sorryAx`.

The witness theorems use the kernel `decide` tactic on concrete values; there
is no `native_decide`.  A scan of the module finds no `sorry`, `admit` or
`native_decide`.

